{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>אם אין</b> — four times in the Masorah: דין (judgment) and the others: \"אם אין אתה\" (if you are not) in connection with Absalom when he counseled him to go out to war against David — \"אם אין אתה שומע לי\" (if you do not listen to me). \"היש בה עץ אם אין\" (is there a tree in it or not). Meaning: I said that it is a good land, and pressed: if you do not listen to me and send spies to see if there is a tree in it or not — by your life, you need to fight, like that אם אין. For Absalom speaks of war, as the Sages said: had they not sent spies, they would not have needed weapons. And so here too, because they said \"היש YHWH בקרבנו אם אין\" (is YHWH among us or not), Amalek came upon them."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ד' במסרה דין ואידך' lists four Masoretic occurrences of אם אין; the first cited is דין and the others follow. The verse reference for היש בה עץ אם אין is Numbers 13:20; for אם אין אתה שומע לי in the Absalom narrative it is 2 Samuel 16:11 — neither address is written by the author."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:22.067162147Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}